{
  "abstract": "For every sufficiently large uniformity r, the closure of the ordinary Turán densities obtained by forbidding one finite r-uniform hypergraph equals the set obtained by forbidding arbitrary families. Both sets consist of zero and the closed interval from r!/r^r to one. Every family density can therefore be approximated to any positive accuracy by forbidding a single hypergraph. The threshold in r is uniform over all families and accuracies.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Xizhi Liu"
    }
  ],
